        sentiment:"Positive",
        topic:"Stock Crosses $1,000 / Supreme Court Whistleblower Ruling",
        summary:"LLY gained ~2.4% and briefly crossed $1,000 mid-week, extending its post-Q1 earnings momentum. The stock dipped Monday alongside pharma peers on the TrumpRx expansion news, then recovered. The Supreme Court declined to hear Lilly's challenge to the False Claims Act's qui tam provision, upholding a judgment from a 2014 Medicaid rebate case brought by whistleblower Ronald Streck — now totaling $220M+ with accrued interest (original verdict was $183M). Lilly also announced a fireside chat with CSO Daniel Skovronsky at Bernstein's Strategic Decisions Conference on May 28.",
        takeaway:"The whistleblower ruling is a known overhang that resolved without meaningful escalation — not a new negative. LLY is now up two straight weeks on clean Q1 execution. The Bernstein conference May 28 is the next event to watch for any color on TrumpRx pricing or pipeline updates.",
        valImpact: false
